\DOC LOCAL_SUB_P384_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_SUB_P384_TAC : int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Advances a symbolic-execution goal through an inlined modular-subtraction
subroutine, replacing the current machine-state assumptions with those for a
later state and adding a conditional assumption characterising the computed
difference modulo the field prime.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument, an {int}, selects which code variant/offset of the
subtraction block to step over. The second, a {string list}, names the result
and the two operand values; these names fix which variables occur in the added
assumption {u1 < p /\ u2 < p ==> &t = (&u1 - &u2) rem &p} and in the
memory-content assumption recording where the result is stored. The conclusion,
an {eventually} statement about a machine state {s}, is rewritten to the same
statement about a fresh successor state {s'}. All assumptions describing the
old state — program-counter value, {bytes_loaded}, register and memory-content
reads, and the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation — are discharged and replaced
by the corresponding assumptions for the new state; the {MAYCHANGE} component
may gain extra written locations, and a new memory-content assumption binds the
named result value at its storage location. The new conditional arithmetic fact
about the named result and operands is added, while previously added facts of
the same kind and the other purely arithmetic side conditions are retained,
sometimes re-asserted in a reordered form.
{
   A ?- eventually ... s
   ================================================  LOCAL_SUB_P384_TAC n ["t"; "u1"; "u2"]
   A' ?- eventually ... s'
}
\noindent where {A'} is the rewritten assumption set described above, including
{u1 < p /\ u2 < p ==> &t = (&u1 - &u2) rem &p}.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single kind of transformation, always on
goals of this symbolic-execution shape.

\ENDDOC
